From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 10:25:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix get_options regressions: advance value pointer and
 escape spaces in options (Issues #1532 and #1630)

Squash of two upstream OpenPrinting/cups fixes to the option-value
string formatting introduced by 8d0f51ca (which this port carries as
backport-filter-control-chars-from-job-options.patch):

  da0ff58c041f7ee129c3c2c72fb14df1f1e4069a (2026-04-08, Issue #1532
  "Fix get_options regression"): the new whitespace branch converted a
  space but did not advance valptr, so any option value containing a
  space (e.g. a document name) made the scheduler loop forever while
  overflowing the options buffer.  Move the increment into the for()
  clause.

  5d72dffab0686dcf3b1b0728702ade46530e2c4b (2026-06-27, Issue #1630
  "Fix escaping of spaces in options", 2.4.x equivalent e966de6d):
  values converted to plain spaces were still re-split into extra
  boolean options by the filters; emit '\' + ' ' so cupsParseOptions
  restores the quoted value (e.g. document-name-supplied="story
  booklet final.pdf" no longer becomes booklet=true, final.pdf=true).

Adaptation: in this port get_options() is refactored into
format_attr_to_buf() by ohos-user-sensitive-options-env.patch, so the
hunks apply to that function with the ptr/valptr naming (upstream
uses optptr).  Allocation note: upstream 0ff88973 ("Expand allocation
of options string") is NOT required here - format_attr_to_buf() keeps
the original tag coverage (no TEXTLANG/NAMELANG/MIMETYPE/URISCHEME)
and ipp_length() reserves 2 * len + 2 per string value, which still
covers the added backslash per whitespace character.

Upstream-commit: da0ff58c041f7ee129c3c2c72fb14df1f1e4069a
Upstream-commit: 5d72dffab0686dcf3b1b0728702ade46530e2c4b


--- a/scheduler/job.c
+++ b/scheduler/job.c
@@ -4333,7 +4333,7 @@
     case IPP_TAG_CHARSET:
     case IPP_TAG_LANGUAGE:
         case IPP_TAG_URI:
-      for (valptr = attr->values[i].string.text; *valptr;)
+      for (valptr = attr->values[i].string.text; *valptr; valptr ++)
       {
        /*
         * Convert tabs and newlines to spaces, filter out control chars,
@@ -4342,13 +4342,18 @@
 
         if (isspace(*valptr & 255))
         {
+         /*
+          * Escape whitespace...
+          */
+
+          *ptr++ = '\\';
           *ptr++ = ' ';
 	}
         else if ((*valptr & 255) >= ' ' && *valptr != 0x7f)
         {
           if (strchr("\\\'\"", *valptr))
 	    *ptr++ = '\\';
-	  *ptr++ = *valptr++;
+	  *ptr++ = *valptr;
 	}
       }
 
